1. Protocol Overview 
Purpose: Is to explain what the system is trying to do — NOT technically, but economically. 

Structure:
- What the protocol is trying to enable
- What problem does it claim to solve
- What environment does it operates in (DeFi, AI agents, infra, etc.)
- Stage (early / growth / scaling)

2. Governance Structure
Purpose: Map who actually controls the system (not limited to what is written in docs).

Structure:
- Decision making authority (who can change what)
- On chain vs off chain governance split
- Admin keys / multisig presence
- Upgrade mechanisms (if any)
- Emergency controls / override logic
Kernel:
Is to focus on "real control vs stated decentralization"

3. Incentive Structure 
Purpose: Describe how the system shapes behavior of users, validators, agents, or capital.

Structure:
- Token distribution model (high-level only)
- Reward mechanisms (staking, liquidity, usage, etc.)
- Participation incentives (why users join)
- Retention incentives (why users stay)
- Exit incentives (why users leave or dump)

Kernel:
Is to conclude on "What behavior is being unintentionally rewarded?”

4. Key Risks
Purpose: Convert the  into visible risk signals 

Kernel:
- Risk: Description
- Mechanism: On why it happens
- Impact: On what breaks

Risk types:
- Governance captures
- Incentive decay 
- Sybil / agent exploitations
- Treasury imbalances
- Upgrade centralizations

5. Systemic Scenario 
Purpose: Simulate how the system breaks under scale without being dramatic 

Kernel:
- Trigger event (growth, listing, exploit, agent scaling)
- Chain reaction (what breaks first, second, third)
- Final system state (what fails completely)
